  "title": "Cao Dai religion",
  "summary": "Cao Dai is a Vietnamese religious movement founded in 1926 by Ngo Van Chieu, a civil administrator in the French colonial government. It was inaugurated on 18 November 1926 in a ceremony drawing some fifty thousand people, and its headquarters is at Tay Ninh. It blends Confucian morality, Buddhist ideas of karma and reincarnation, and Daoist occultism.",
